        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "9b959db1-1b9e-3612-bd99-fd56e59519a2",
                "word": "bredouille",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ed718765-25e4-49d4-b213-bba35df01fa8",
                        "entry_id": "9b959db1-1b9e-3612-bd99-fd56e59519a2",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bredouilles"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eb987467-ba9a-39e0-92f9-dc98951b59cc",
                        "entry_id": "9b959db1-1b9e-3612-bd99-fd56e59519a2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualifie une personne qui échoue à parvenir à son but."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5692c456-0d76-48d2-b144-467bb6f53e0c",
                                "sense_id": "eb987467-ba9a-39e0-92f9-dc98951b59cc",
                                "text": "Il n’a peut-être pas dîné, le duc ; il est sans doute revenu bredouille de ses quotidiennes tournées au café Anglais, à la Maison Dorée, chez Bignon, en quête d’un ami et d’un menu."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0b8a6d3-4ac2-4a58-98c3-ddd600809d70",
                                "sense_id": "eb987467-ba9a-39e0-92f9-dc98951b59cc",
                                "text": "Bref, bredouille la maréchaussée, autant que pour un voleur ou un contrebandier ! On y était bien habitué, allez : pas de semaines qu'une poule disparaisse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d08f5bcd-4428-48c9-9366-cc8413ca4662",
                                "sense_id": "eb987467-ba9a-39e0-92f9-dc98951b59cc",
                                "text": "Au XVIe siècle, la France, qui s'était lancée dans un conflit avec les Italiens, revient défaite, mais pas bredouille."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c5774d20-5503-48c8-b32f-fdf7bc41061e",
                                "sense_id": "eb987467-ba9a-39e0-92f9-dc98951b59cc",
                                "text": "Être bredouille, perdre la partie sans faire un seul point, être complètement battu."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ffd3795-dc45-490d-8a5d-31e0a69ba810",
                                "sense_id": "eb987467-ba9a-39e0-92f9-dc98951b59cc",
                                "text": "Sortir bredouille d’un lieu, d’une assemblée, en sortir sans avoir pu rien faire de ce qu’on s’était proposé."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "41359322-fa65-41ae-9292-5e57810f4864",
                                "sense_id": "eb987467-ba9a-39e0-92f9-dc98951b59cc",
                                "text": "Revenir bredouille de la chasse, n’avoir rien tué."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f16a7765-b3c2-4c1e-b44e-a099c2345ced",
                                "sense_id": "eb987467-ba9a-39e0-92f9-dc98951b59cc",
                                "text": "Et alors ? On est bredouille ! Et puis, la chasse c’est une bonne chose pour un Zoulou, la meilleure qui soit après la guerre."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2caee197-dacc-459b-ac66-d2f1f5a6312c",
                        "source_entry_id": "9b959db1-1b9e-3612-bd99-fd56e59519a2",
                        "source_sense_id": "eb987467-ba9a-39e0-92f9-dc98951b59cc",
                        "source_sense_description": "Qui échoue à parvenir à son but",
                        "target_lang_word": "emptyhanded",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "emptyhanded",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6c737705-d1b6-34a6-87e8-0dd43fa7bfea",
                                        "entry_id": "046e9dec-24f6-3538-a03a-633721730915",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "With nothing in one's hands."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad6519b3-dd97-4582-ae19-e32f7f352ec4",
                                                "sense_id": "6c737705-d1b6-34a6-87e8-0dd43fa7bfea",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: unburdened, unencumbered, unladen"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0941b561-f6bf-4c9c-bd45-685df95c4140",
                                                "sense_id": "6c737705-d1b6-34a6-87e8-0dd43fa7bfea",
                                                "text": "If, for example, Oswald was not \"emptyhanded\" but, as the original reports had it, had been drinking a Coca-Cola — there was a vending machine in the lunchroom where the encounter occurred — then he almost certainly could not have left the sixth-floor window after firing the shots, hid the rifle on the sixth floor, run down to the second floor, entered the lunchroom, operated the machine, ..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c97b2ad5-0afb-3482-b1c0-1a986a22c3e2",
                                        "entry_id": "046e9dec-24f6-3538-a03a-633721730915",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Impoverished; having no money or resources."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91717cae-88fd-4477-944d-3d59551e95db",
                                                "sense_id": "c97b2ad5-0afb-3482-b1c0-1a986a22c3e2",
                                                "text": "As he walked about in the village, Isaac saw those inhabitants who had come to the Land emptyhanded and now own fields and vineyards and houses full of good things, not by virtue of observing the Torah and pious deeds, for the Biluim were free thinkers and their feet too are on the ground, but because they're Russians and I'm from Galicia, and even the one small village the Galicians put up fell to rack and ruin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5ee9b541-1e80-356a-b733-28706a1ec2f6",
                                        "entry_id": "046e9dec-24f6-3538-a03a-633721730915",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having nothing to offer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0be845e1-4ed1-4dc3-ac88-050be993acd1",
                                                "sense_id": "5ee9b541-1e80-356a-b733-28706a1ec2f6",
                                                "text": "I come to this conference bearing neither a new slogan nor a basket full of gifts. But I do not come emptyhanded. I come with the promise of the Government and people of the United States to work with you..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "965ec80d-7d0f-3182-bf16-801ba0b2c741",
                                        "entry_id": "046e9dec-24f6-3538-a03a-633721730915",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having received or acquired nothing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1c8d6c8-b5a3-4961-ae72-baa1ae4de7ae",
                                                "sense_id": "965ec80d-7d0f-3182-bf16-801ba0b2c741",
                                                "text": "Returning \"emptyhanded\" doesn't always mean that you didn't get what you set out for."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af0f5764-d35f-4fad-b314-204565cc9b53",
                                                "sense_id": "965ec80d-7d0f-3182-bf16-801ba0b2c741",
                                                "text": "\"Have you got anything, my dear? If you are emptyhanded, go emptyhanded.\" But the shopper said, \"Sisters, stop teasing him, for by God, he served me well today; no one else would have been as patient with me. Whatever his share will come to, I shall pay for him myself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "345d8221-361a-4b49-8029-9aba713d10cc",
                                                "sense_id": "965ec80d-7d0f-3182-bf16-801ba0b2c741",
                                                "text": "Antar neglected his boat and his nets for three days on end, and when, on the entreaties of his wife and children, he brought himself to go back to sea, he came back in the evening emptyhanded."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43c5dc10-b5f1-3688-bbb8-40cc8062af77",
                                        "entry_id": "046e9dec-24f6-3538-a03a-633721730915",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having nothing to offer; unable to give what was promised."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0af2a9e8-7367-4869-a88f-81eede69785e",
                                                "sense_id": "43c5dc10-b5f1-3688-bbb8-40cc8062af77",
                                                "text": "...he promised to get concessions on container handling, and he cannot go to the dockers emptyhanded."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29d09697-69f4-40e6-ab3a-11615af61092",
                                                "sense_id": "43c5dc10-b5f1-3688-bbb8-40cc8062af77",
                                                "text": "We want to make them aware of all of the programs so these people don't go home emptyhanded. Many times they go home emptyhanded because the person has been trained with the tunnel vision where he is thinking only of the one program and is not aware of the other programs that exist, and this is what we have been doing this last year is trying to cross train our people and at least if nothing else have some communication."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ca2ec7a5-fc03-35eb-8061-1721df770167",
                                        "entry_id": "046e9dec-24f6-3538-a03a-633721730915",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unarmed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34eef685-37f1-4599-9b7a-057733dedf46",
                                                "sense_id": "ca2ec7a5-fc03-35eb-8061-1721df770167",
                                                "text": "...for he has come on an ambassage and he has come emptyhanded (not armed)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3d7c2b45-1a46-449f-96ff-171dbf537e2c",
                        "source_entry_id": "9b959db1-1b9e-3612-bd99-fd56e59519a2",
